    "code":  "GONOCOCCAL_URETHRITIS",
    "name":  "Gonococcal urethritis",
    "module":  "male-genital",
    "category":  "disease",
    "description":  "Gonococcal urethritis is inflammation of the urethra caused by Neisseria gonorrhoeae, a gram-negative diplococcus. It is one of the most common sexually transmitted infections worldwide. In men, it typically presents with a profuse, purulent or mucopurulent urethral discharge and dysuria, usually appearing 2–7 days after exposure. Asymptomatic infection is less common in men than women but can occur. Untreated infection may ascend to cause epididymo-orchitis, prostatitis, or disseminated gonococcal infection (DGI) with arthritis, tenosynovitis, and skin lesions. Treatment requires dual therapy due to increasing antibiotic resistance; partner notification and testing are mandatory.",
